          "text": "# Durable & Reusable Learnings\n\n## Operator Preferences\n- **Model-Agnostic Adaptation**: The operator swaps between different models frequently to manage and optimize costs. System configurations, boundaries, and logic must be robust across diverse model architectures rather than overly tailored to a single option.\n- **Terse Output Formatting**: Output tokens are often overly descriptive and should be far more terse. Future developments must prioritize output format efficiency, specifically starting with prefix reduction in autoresearch and progressive disclosure improvements.\n- **Focus on Response Format**: The core goal is using autoresearch to improve progressive disclosure response format efficiency. Keep compression levels as-is and target other vectors for output verbosity.\n- **Flexibility and Token Efficiency**: Keep a strong balance between context flexibility and token efficiency, especially for longer, more complex dynamic workflows in pi.\n\n## Confirmed Gotchas & Facts\n- **Context Pruning Explosion**: Entering every-turn mode with `pi-context-prune` was a critical failure. It exploded requests (from 4-5 up to 12-27 per loop) and increased total token consumption by 6x; thus, rapid reversion is required for this mode.\n- **Schema Optimization via Truncation**: Setting `aggressiveMaxDescChars=30` in `tscg.json` is highly effective. It reduces description overhead by ~22% (saving ~14,676 tokens per request, reducing total median across benchmarks from ~73k to ~58k tokens).\n- **Model Destabilization via Configuration**: Custom adjustments to lean-ctx footers (`LEAN_CTX_SAVINGS_FOOTER` and `LEAN_CTX_AGGRESSIVENESS`) had negligible utility (~30 tokens saved) but heavily destabilized model behavior.\n- **Tool Disablement for Context Efficacy**: Disabling high-overhead but unnecessary tools globally via `pi-lean-ctx` (`disableTools`: `ctx_doctor`, `ctx_insight`, `ctx_stats`, `ctx_upgrade`, `ctx_purge`) saves ~93 tokens on probe, yielding around ~... [truncated]",
